{"id": "unknown-2026-08-10-008", "date": "2026-08-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU formaldehyde rule tests $9 bn carpet and curtain trade", "content": "EU REACH Entry 77 applies an emissions ceiling of 0.080 mg/m³, making carpets and textile floor coverings the clearest textile category exposed.\nTexPro puts 2025 European imports of carpets, textile floor coverings and curtains at $9.04 billion, up 5.9 per cent.\nChina leads at $1.60 billion; India’s exposure is 94.6 per cent carpets/floor coverings, while Türkiye supplies $984.9 million.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eu-formaldehyde-rule-tests-9-bn-carpet-and-curtain-trade-312496-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-10-009", "date": "2026-08-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["increase"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "What drove India’s PDS revenue up 15% in Q1 FY27?", "content": "PDS Limited has reported a strong Q1 FY27, with revenue rising 14.8 per cent YoY to ₹3,444 crore (~$344.4 million) and PAT increasing 42.7 per cent to ₹29 crore (~$2.9 million). \nGMV grew 11.1 per cent to ₹5,146 crore (~$514.6 million), while EBITDA surged 90.2 per cent to ₹96 crore (~$9.6 million). \nThe order book increased 23 per cent YoY to ₹6,095 crore (~$9.6 million). ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/what-drove-india-s-pds-revenue-up-15-in-q1-fy27--312501-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-10-010", "date": "2026-08-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["leading"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "China water-jet deliveries fall 57% as India leads rapier investment", "content": "India became the leading destination for rapier/projectile looms in 2025, with deliveries rising 21 per cent.\nTexPro shows China exported $38.76 billion of selected woven fabrics in 2025 against India’s $3.60 billion, a 10.8-fold gap.\nChina’s selected woven-fabric exports to India rose 11.6 per cent in 2025 and surged 28.3 per cent in January–April 2026.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-water-jet-deliveries-fall-57-as-india-leads-rapier-investment-312495-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-10-011", "date": "2026-08-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "FUTA Express, VET strengthen Vietnam-Cambodia cargo connectivity", "content": "FUTA Express and VET have signed an MoU to expand Vietnam-Cambodia logistics, covering two-way cargo flows and operating integration.  \nThe cooperation will connect warehouses, vehicles, delivery points and processes, with more technology for tracking and cargo control. \nFresh, seasonal and temperature-controlled goods are a focus, with partners aiming to cut delivery times and costs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/futa-express-vet-strengthen-vietnam-cambodia-cargo-connectivity-312488-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-10-012", "date": "2026-08-10", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "China machinery value added rises 6.4% in H1", "content": "China's major machinery enterprises posted 6.4 per cent growth in value added in H1 2026, ahead of broader industry and manufacturing.\nRevenue rose 6.5 per cent to 16.1 trillion yuan (~$2.38 trillion), with output growth in 80 of 127 monitored products.\nSmart equipment, industrial robots and high-end machine tools point to firmer automation demand.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-machinery-value-added-rises-6-4-in-h1-312486-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
